10
00:46:18,947 --> 00:46:24,947
Meat Loaf: In Search of Paradise is a 2007 independent documentary film that captures rocker
Meat Loaf and his life in rehearsals and on the road during his 2007 World Tour.

11
00:50:56,842 --> 00:51:02,842
It was directed by Bruce David Klein and produced by Bruce David
Klein and Paulina Vera Williams by Atlas Media Corp.

12
00:55:34,736 --> 00:55:40,736
in association with Voom HD Pictures and 10th Street Entertainment.

13
01:00:12,631 --> 01:00:18,631
The film was an official selection of the Montreal World Film
Festival in 2007 and of the USA Film Festival in 2008.

14
01:04:50,526 --> 01:04:56,526
In Europe, the film was included in the 3 Bats Live DVD.

15
01:09:28,421 --> 01:09:34,421
According to Allmovie, "as the stage show gets more and more involved, the singer battles
ongoing health concerns."
The film was theatrically released in 75 cities in the U.S.

16
01:14:06,315 --> 01:14:12,315
and Canada on March 12, 2008.

17
01:18:44,210 --> 01:18:50,210
The premiere was held at New York City's IFC Center.

18
01:23:22,105 --> 01:23:28,105
The New York Times called the film "amusing," and Variety said it was "revealing."  It is
now available on DVD from Universal and can be seen on television worldwide.
